  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: With only two completed experiments, RNA-only (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% accuracy while image-only (resnet50, singleprofile) achieves just 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality but leaving the multiprofile question entirely untested. Question: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) directly tests whether aggregating multiple cell profiles per sample improves over a single profile, using the simplest aggregation (average pooling) to isolate the profile-count effect from aggregation complexity. Why this is the best next experiment: The multiprofile decision is a structural axis that governs ~24 of the 51 remaining configurations. If multiprofile provides no gain over singleprofile, a large portion of the search space can be deprioritized; if it does help, it validates investing in more sophisticated aggregations (transformer) and encoders (scvi, scgpt) under the multiprofile setting. This experiment is a clean, minimal extension of config_001 (same modality, same encoder) and thus maximally informative per unit budget under the current sparse evidence."
}

